# web-page-design — Trae .rules
# Place this file at the root of your project as `.rules`
# or merge its contents into your existing .rules file.
#
# These rules configure Trae's agent behavior specifically
# for web page design tasks.

## Stack preferences
- Always output valid semantic HTML5 with a CSS reset
- Default to vanilla HTML/CSS/JS unless the user specifies a framework
- If a framework is requested, prefer: Next.js > Astro > plain React
- Always use CSS custom properties (variables) for colors, fonts, and spacing
- Always import Google Fonts via <link> — never use system/generic fonts

## Design rules
- Never use Inter, Roboto, or Arial as display/headline fonts
- Always provide mobile-first responsive styles (min-width breakpoints)
- Every page must have a clear primary CTA above the fold
- Minimum body font size: 16px
- Always include :hover and :focus states on interactive elements

## Code quality
- Use semantic HTML tags: <header>, <nav>, <main>, <section>, <footer>
- Include alt text on all images
- All images below the hero must use loading="lazy"
- Include <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
- Add <!-- Section: [name] --> comments before each major section

## Agent behavior
- When given a vague request ("make me a website"), ask for: purpose, audience, and key CTA before generating
- When given a screenshot or mockup, extract the color palette and typography before rebuilding
- Always output a single self-contained file unless the user requests a multi-file project
- After generating, summarize: aesthetic direction chosen, fonts used, color palette, and sections included
